@@ -9,6 +9,23 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Agent tools
+
+The sign-in and sign-up forms expose `sign_in` and `sign_up`, respectively,
+through [WebMCP](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api)
+when mounted on their pages. Both accept an object with required `username`
+and `password` strings. They submit to the same endpoints and update the same
+loading, error, and success messages as manual submissions. Registration clears
+the fields on success. Results are JSON strings containing `{ ok, message }`;
+credentials and authentication tokens are never included in tool results.
+
+Use a browser with WebMCP enabled on HTTPS or localhost. The integration detects
+`document.modelContext` and supports the older `navigator.modelContext` API.
+Tools are removed when the form unmounts. Browsers without WebMCP keep the normal
+forms available.
+
+Run automated checks with `pnpm test` (Node.js 24+) and `pnpm build`.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
